    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All tests pass \u2014 **58 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented owner deletion as a soft-delete. The changes:\n\n**1. `Owner` entity** (`model/Owner.java`) \u2014 added a `deleted` boolean field (column `deleted`, `NOT NULL`) with `isDeleted()`/`setDeleted(...)`. A new owner defaults to `false`.\n\n**2. OpenAPI spec** (`resources/openapi.yml`) \u2014 added a read-only `deleted` boolean to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes it and MapStruct maps it automatically. `GET /api/owners/{id}` now returns `\"deleted\": false`/`true`.\n\n**3. Controller** (`OwnerRestControllerV1.deleteOwner`) \u2014 instead of removing the record, it sets `deleted = true` and calls `saveOwner(...)`, returning `204` (2xx). The row is retained, so `GET` still returns the owner afterward with `deleted: true`.\n\n**4. Create-time duplicate/identity checks** \u2014 `rejectDuplicateIdentity` (the blocking telephone/email/household check) and `findPossibleDuplicateOf` now skip owners flagged `deleted`, so a normally-blocking duplicate is allowed when the only matching owner has been soft-deleted.\n\n**5. DB schema** \u2014 added the `deleted` column (default false, not null) to all four `schema.sql` files (hsqldb, h2, postgres with `DEFAULT FALSE NOT NULL` ordering that HSQLDB requires; mysql as `BIT(1) NOT NULL DEFAULT 0`), since `ddl-auto=none` means the schema is script-driven. Existing seed rows default to `false`.\n\nBoth new `Cp46Tests` cases (soft-delete flags-and-retains, and deleted owner ignored by the duplicate check) pass, along with the full existing suite.",
